  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1118 AM CDT Sun Oct 25 2026\n\nWarm and dry conditions will continue to impact the Mid-South\nthis week as a 592 dam ridge remains parked over central CONUS.\nDiurnal temperature ranges will vary widely each day with highs\nin the upper 70s and lows in the lower 50s. A few shortwaves will\npass north of the forecast area by midweek, but no significant\nweather changes are anticipated due to a lack of moisture in the\natmospheric column. These prolonged dry conditions, combined with\nrelative humidity around 30 percent, will elevate fire weather\nconcerns through at least midweek.\n\nBy the end of the week, a subtropical jet will move across the\nsouthern Plains. This feature may bring increased moisture into\nour area, allowing rain chances to increase over the weekend.\nWhile this means potential rain on Halloween, it would also mark\nan end to our prolonged dry spell. Ultimately, guidance depicts\nless than 1 inch of rain falling this upcoming weekend. While not\nmuch, any precipitation is welcomed.",
